  "answer_text": "Because \"Glenwood Pool\" can refer to several different notable pools across the United States, here is information on the most prominent locations to help you find the one you are looking for:\n\n### 1. Glenwood Hot Springs Pool (Glenwood Springs, Colorado)\nThis is the most famous \"Glenwood Pool\" in the world. Located in western Colorado along I-70, it is the **world's largest mineral hot springs pool**.\n* **Key Features:** Fed by the Yampah Spring (producing over 3.5 million gallons of 122\u00b0F water daily, which is cooled for safe soaking). It features the **Grand Pool** (kept at 90\u201393\u00b0F), a **Therapy Pool** (kept at 104\u00b0F), and the family-friendly **Sopris Splash Zone** (which includes a river tube ride and splash pad).\n* **Access:** Open year-round to the public (daily passes are required) and free for guests staying at the Glenwood Hot Springs Lodge. \n* **Location:** 415 E. 6th St., Glenwood Springs, CO 81601.\n\n### 2. Glenwood Pool / Recreation Club (Silver Spring, Maryland)\nA highly popular community-owned, non-profit swim club nestled in a wooded glen in the historic Forest Glen neighborhood.\n* **Key Features:** Features a 25-meter L-shaped pool with a 13-foot deep diving well, a beach-entry shallow area with a \"tea cup\" water feature, and a separate fenced wading pool. It is also home to the Glenwood Tigers swim and dive teams.\n* **Access:** Private membership-based club, though open to the public to join (often with a waitlist).\n* **Location:** 10012 Gardiner Ave, Silver Spring, MD 20902.\n\n### 3. Glenwood Park Pool (Atlanta, Georgia)\nLocated in the award-winning, EarthCraft-certified \"New Urbanist\" neighborhood of Glenwood Park near Grant Park.\n* **Key Features:** A 6-lane, Junior Olympic-sized saline pool with an adjacent kids' water play area, a picnic area with a grill, and a local swim team (the Piranhas).\n* **Access:** Membership is open to neighborhood residents (and some non-residents depending on availability).\n* **Location:** 943 North Ormewood Park Drive SE, Atlanta, GA 30316.\n\n### 4. Glenwood Pool (Columbus, Ohio)\nA public municipal pool managed by the Columbus Recreation and Parks Department.\n* **Key Features:** An outdoor public pool that opens seasonally around Memorial Day weekend through the summer. \n* **Access:** Open to the public. Admission requires a Columbus Recreation and Parks Leisure Card (which is free to obtain) plus a daily entry fee or season pass. \n* **Location:** Columbus, OH.\n\n### 5. Glenwood Park YMCA Pool (Erie, Pennsylvania)\nA regional recreational pool facility operated by the YMCA of Greater Erie.\n* **Key Features:** Features large indoor/outdoor pools hosting open swims, lap swimming, and water fitness classes.\n* **Access:** Free for YMCA members; day passes are available for non-members.\n* **Location:** 3727 Cherry Street, Erie, PA 16508.\n\n***\n\n*If you are looking for specific details like **hours of operation, membership pricing, or current schedules** for one of these pools, please reply with the city or state you are interested in!*",
